From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: keep PD_VI on while the
 camera is powered

CLK_CIF_OUT, CLK_CAM0_OUT and CLK_CAM1_OUT are all generated inside the VI
power domain, and the clock framework has no idea. With PD_VI powered down
the gate bit in CRU_CLKGATE_CON19 reads back as ungated, clk_get_rate()
returns the expected 24 MHz and clk_summary shows "hardware enable = Y", but
no clock reaches the pin.

Measured by sampling the GPIO4 EXT_PORT register with the clkout muxed onto
its pin:

  PD_VI off: the pad reads 0 in 20 of 20 samples
  PD_VI on:  the pad reads 0 in 12 and 1 in 8 of 20 samples

(The same pin driven as a plain GPIO follows the output register in both
directions, so the pad and its input buffer are fine.)

The sensor enables its XVCLK from its runtime-resume callback, long before
anything resumes VICAP or the CSI-2 receiver, so it never saw a clock.
Rockchip's own BSP puts power-domains on every camera sensor node for this
reason; do the same.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN f2_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi f2_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 09:29:58.350036673 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 09:29:58.350140419 +0200
@@ -630,6 +630,14 @@
 		assigned-clocks = <&cru CLK_CIF_OUT>;
 		assigned-clock-rates = <24000000>;
 
+		/*
+		 * CLK_CIF_OUT is generated inside the VI power domain. Its
+		 * gate register reads back as enabled while that domain is
+		 * off, but no clock reaches the pin, so claim the domain for
+		 * as long as the sensor is powered.
+		 */
+		power-domains = <&power RK3568_PD_VI>;
+
 		avdd-supply = <&vcc2v8_dvp>;
 		dvdd-supply = <&vdd1v2_dvp>;
 		dovdd-supply = <&vcc1v8_dvp>;
